# What this image is expected to contain. Checked at build time by
# restaurant/patches/assert_pins.py — a mismatch fails the bake loudly rather
# than shipping a silently different app. deploy.sh reads the frappe pin from
# here, so this file is the one place a version changes.
#
# Keep erpnext and hrms current together. hrms from v16.5.1 writes to
# Accounts Settings.repost_allowed_types, which erpnext only grew later, so an
# old erpnext with a current hrms fails install-app with AttributeError. The
# pairing below is the tested one.
#
# frappe is pinned to a tag rather than the moving version-16 branch: the tag
# names both the app clone and the frappe/build + frappe/base image tags.
#
# erpnext-restaurant has NO tags upstream and bench clones with --branch, which
# will not take a bare SHA, so master is asserted instead. To convert that into
# a true pin: fork alphabit-technology/erpnext-restaurant, tag this commit, and
# point apps-restaurant.json at the fork + tag.
frappe=v16.31.0
erpnext=v16.32.3
hrms=v16.16.0
restaurant_management=c55ac4ae84810be445b4895089516e12a299ba9a
